      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)+⟨2,\\,1,\\,3⟩\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-4,\\,-5,\\,1⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-4,\\,-5,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,5,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)+⟨2,\\,1,\\,3⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨2,\\,1,\\,3⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,5,\\,-1⟩+{⟨2t,\\,t,\\,3t⟩|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,5,\\,-1⟩+⟨4,\\,2,\\,6⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨8,\\,7,\\,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
